{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And he did not recognize him, etc.</b> Nevertheless, he set aside the hearing of the voice in favor of the sense of touch, for the voice can change — whether on the side of the one producing the sound or on the side of the one hearing it — whereas the feel of the hairs of the hands is a clear sign." "<b>And he blessed him.</b> Meaning: for from the time he first felt him and knew that it was Esav, he had nothing to contradict the voice that came to his ears telling him it was not Esav — and this would mislead him and lead him into the suspicion of Yaakov, who had said ״I would bring upon myself,״ etc. And even though we do not find that he cursed him, nevertheless he prepared his heart to hate him — and this matter has effect among the righteous. Go out and learn from the words of our Sages of blessed memory (Bava Metzia 84a): if they had been insistent in their hearts against another, they would have brought a curse upon him. Therefore, when he saw that his hands were hairy, <b>he blessed him</b>, to remove the opposite effect that had been drawn down previously."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:50.527458561Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}